  "regla": "Centuries are written with Roman numerals after siglo (el siglo XXI) and read as ordinary cardinal numbers: el siglo veintiuno, el siglo quince. From I to X you'll also hear ordinals: el siglo primero, el siglo quinto.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "In Spanish, centuries are written with **Roman numerals** in capitals, after the word **siglo**: **el siglo XX, el siglo XXI**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Read them as **cardinal numbers** (uno, dos, tres…): **el siglo XIX** = **el siglo diecinueve**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Written",
            "Said",
            "Years"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "siglo V",
              "siglo cinco / quinto",
              "401–500"
            ],
            [
              "siglo XV",
              "siglo quince",
              "1401–1500"
            ],
            [
              "siglo XVIII",
              "siglo dieciocho",
              "1701–1800"
            ],
            [
              "siglo XX",
              "siglo veinte",
              "1901–2000"
            ],
            [
              "siglo XXI",
              "siglo veintiuno",
              "2001–2100"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "From I to X, ordinals are common too: **el siglo primero, el siglo quinto**. From XI on, use cardinals."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "As in English, the century is one ahead of the year: the 1900s are **el siglo XX**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Useful phrases: **en el siglo XIX** (_in the 19th century_), **a principios del siglo XX** (_at the start of_), **a finales del siglo XVIII** (_at the end of_). For BC / AD: **a. C.** / **d. C.**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Popes and kings use Roman numerals too, read the same way: **Benedicto XVI** (dieciséis), **Luis XIV** (catorce), **Juan Pablo II** (segundo)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: write it Roman, say it normal."
        }
      ]
    },
